 # DecoSwap
 
-DecoSwap 0.1.17 is a Paper plugin for capturing exact blocks and entities as reusable Decorations, organizing them into Groups, and deploying them with a fresh rollback Snapshot. Separate runtime exports target Paper 1.21.4–1.21.11, 26.1.x, 26.2.x, and 26.3.x.
+DecoSwap 0.1.18 is a Paper plugin for capturing exact blocks and entities as reusable Decorations, organizing them into Groups, and deploying them with a fresh rollback Snapshot. Separate runtime exports target Paper 1.21.4–1.21.11, 26.1.x, 26.2.x, and 26.3.x.
 
 Created by [MrDinoCarlos](https://github.com/MrDinoCarlos) · [mrdino.es](https://mrdino.es/) · [GitHub](https://github.com/MrDinoCarlos)
 
 ## Requirements
+
+XmasLights 2.7+ is an optional integration. Selecting one visible light part captures its entire segment with its logical state. Placement creates independent, animated copies and supports rotation, regeneration and rollback. RGB carriers and owned native LIGHT blocks remain temporary effects. Both plugins must be updated to preserve working lights; older templates containing only XmasLights displays must be saved again. No extra controller entity or hard dependency is added.
+
 
 - The export matching your Paper family: 1.21.4–1.21.11, 26.1.x, 26.2.x, or 26.3.x
 - Java 21+ for the 1.21 export; Java 25+ for the 26.x exports
